/-!
This fragment is intended to be appended after
`P3_Local_Friedrichs_Approximation_Closure_Fragment.lean`.

The earlier local graph-limit theorems deliberately hid the planar test
sequence after transferring its Cauchy property to the Petersson space.
For global quotient-compatible gluing one also needs that sequence: its
literal reduced-chart gauge model identifies the global Petersson limit by
pairing, without any injectivity assertion for chart restriction.  The two
theorems below expose the physical core sequence and its planar gauge models
simultaneously.
-/

namespace Mock2FA.PaperCorrections.AutomorphicSobolev
namespace FixedPhaseReducedChartFriedrichs

open Set Function Topology Filter MeasureTheory Metric
open scoped BigOperators
open HalfIntegralMultiplier
