/-!
This fragment is intended after, in order,

* `P3_Reduced_Chart_Periodization_Closure_Fragment.lean`,
* `P3_Planar_Localization_Closure_Fragment.lean`,
* `P3_Essential_Support_Buffer_Closure_Fragment.lean`,
* `P3_Reduced_Chart_L2_Descent_Closure_Fragment.lean`,
* `P3_Reduced_Chart_Weak_Graph_Closure_Fragment.lean`,
* `P3_Local_Friedrichs_Approximation_Closure_Fragment.lean`,
* `P3_Exposed_Local_Model_Graph_Limit_Fragment.lean`,
* `P3_Quotient_Compatible_Finite_Gluing_Fragment.lean`,
* `P3_Invariant_Scalar_Multiplier_Closure_Fragment.lean`, and
* `P3_Quotient_Local_Multiplier_Pairing_Closure_Fragment.lean`.

It closes the two compact Friedrichs-periodization obligations without an
analytic certificate.  The base coordinate of every local periodized limit
is identified globally by completed Petersson pairings.  The derivative
coordinates are not reconstructed by a formal differentiation of a
partition of unity: they are identified by closedness and single-valuedness
of the opposite maximal-adjoint graph.  This avoids both the false
injectivity of chart restriction and a hidden seam-derivative premise.
-/

